zl1 -- the SECOND heat cause (cpufreq governor), the ALTERNATING design, SIX device runs, 2026-09-26
====================================================================================================

ONE BOOT THROUGHOUT: boot_id 2fbf9f8e-deea-4955-ad0c-6bddf0fb14f5 -- the same boot as docs 168, 170,
172, 173 and 174. Re-read before the first run and after the last: UNCHANGED. Four cores read
`interactive` after every run (each run's own trap restores it and re-reads it). Nothing was
flashed, no partition was written, no block device was opened, no service was restarted, the
container was never stopped. The instrument (/tmp/zl1-governor-temp-ab.sh, md5
a148b614c35e59c640676c5f27c7b368) was copied to /tmp and its md5 compared with the host's copy
before the first run: identical.

WHAT WAS RUN. The alternating design (docs 175) on the real phone, six times, to answer the one
question docs 175's closing line names: how big is THIS phone's scatter. Runs 1-4 and 6 are the
design's own defaults (30 s windows, 5 s settle); run 5 takes the same design with 90 s windows to
test whether the window length moves the answer.

THE HEADLINE, AND IT IS NOT A PRICE. The same design on the same phone on the same boot printed
+2.03, -0.58, +2.48, +5.88, +2.27 and +2.30 C -- on FOUR DIFFERENT 'primary' zones, because the
pre-registered zone is the hottest sensor of window A.1 and that changes hands between runs. An
independent 2 s by-name sampler running beside run 6 (reading /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/temp
by NAME, no column arithmetic, its timestamps from /proc/uptime) gives a THIRD answer for the same
windows: window MEANS instead of the instrument's single end-of-window snapshot, section 7 below.

VERDICT BODY PER RUN
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


